The commit of the IMAS-Fortran HLI that .github/workflows/hli-validation.yml
builds against the installed shim. First line only is the value, the way
CMakeLists.txt reads IMAS_CORE_VERSION with LIMIT_COUNT 1; everything below it
is commentary.

A full commit SHA rather than a branch. It is the build cache's key, and it is
what makes a red HLI job attributable: a moved HLI shows up as a one-line diff
to this file in the same pull request, so a failure that arrives without one is
the shim's or upstream IMAS-Core's. See
docs/adr/0020-hli-validation-floats-core-and-pins-the-dd.md.

Repository: https://github.com/yohannmarguier/IMAS-Fortran (branch develop as
of this commit). The repository name lives in the workflow rather than here,
because it is not the part that moves. Upstream IMAS-Fortran carries no
AL_USE_MULTIVERSION_SHIM option, so the fork is not a convenience.

To move the pin: check that the fork commit still builds with
AL_USE_MULTIVERSION_SHIM=ON and DD_VERSION=4.1.1, then update the first line.
Bumping this invalidates the build cache by design, so expect the next run to
take the full cold-build time rather than the warm one.
